From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] win32: do not force-enable dvdread and caca

The win32 build.sh force-appends `--enable-dvdread --enable-caca` for desktop
(non-WinStore) builds, after any caller-provided CONFIGFLAGS, so a trailing
`--disable-dvdread` cannot win. We build a minimal contrib closure without
libdvdread or libcaca, and those modules then hard-error at configure. Drop the
forced enables; callers that want them can pass --enable-dvdread/--enable-caca.
---
 extras/package/win32/build.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extras/package/win32/build.sh b/extras/package/win32/build.sh
--- a/extras/package/win32/build.sh
+++ b/extras/package/win32/build.sh
@@ -505,7 +505,7 @@ if [ -n "$WINSTORE" ]; then
     CONFIGFLAGS="$CONFIGFLAGS --disable-crystalhd --disable-dxva2"
 
 else
-    CONFIGFLAGS="$CONFIGFLAGS --enable-dvdread --enable-caca"
+    :
 fi
 if [ -n "$INSTALL_PATH" ]; then
     CONFIGFLAGS="$CONFIGFLAGS --prefix=$INSTALL_PATH"
